      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that when a CSV format has 3 duplicate header names (with the last mapped to index 2), accessing a record by that header name throws `IllegalArgumentException` if the record has fewer values than the header index. Let me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts the duplicate header name into a named constant, uses a fluent builder chain for clarity, and adds comments explaining why duplicate headers cause the index/size mismatch that triggers the `IllegalArgumentException`."
